WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.000
Hello everybody, my name is Markiplier, and welcome back to Subnautica.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.940
Now I wanted to thank you guys so much for all of your patience in getting this series back on its feet.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:08.580
*Occasional Sea Dragon Noises*

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.200
We were in Boston a lot longer then we thought we were going to be

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.600
and we planned to be there a lot longer-

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:18.200
Ignore the, the dragon that's outside of my doors trying to get into this boat.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.880
Uh, he's an unfriendly neighbor because I'm about to move into the neighborhood here.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:28.160
Uh, but I just wanted to thank you guys for being so patient and I understand that I left this on a cliffhanger

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:33.460
with, the, uh, research base to explore and the other things that I have in mind.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.200
But first things first, Thank you Moonshine for commenting,

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:42.880
"You got a signal for the alien thermal plant which is a precursor base inside the lava castle,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.220
so the spire formation that you were fighting the sea dragon above with the smoke"-

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:53.300
I like how you say I was "FIGHTING" the sea dragon and not being "MAULED TO DEATH" by the sea dragon.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:59.800
Being "BEATEN ALIVE" and then "EATEN ALIVE" and then "SHITTEN ALIVE" out into the lava zone,

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:07.100
Uh, and then magically I managed to respawn back into my, my cyclops here, which is a blessing to be sure.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:11.000
Um, but this base is NOT the containment facility.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.060
That is in the active lava zone.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:17.500
Apparently I'm not in the "active" lava zone.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:22.700
So as some of you may have already known, and as I was rambling on about in the livestream yesterday for about 10 years,

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:23.260
I'm sick.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:25.160
I have the flu,

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:29.800
and Amy now has the flu too, and she was so nice to take care of me while I was sick,

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:33.900
and then she got the flu, so I am going to me taking care of her while she recovers.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.660
But I did get some time to record this.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:40.680
Uh so I also want to thank Ethan Garak who said in the inactive lava zone,

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.920
multiple reaper leviathans skeletons can be found.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.680
This is due to sea dragons coming up from the lava zone to catch them,

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:50.220
then drag them down to the lava zone to feast.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.900
That's a horrifying thought,

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.860
because if the dragon's only diet is reaper leviathans, then what chance do I have?

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.720
Why in the hell did I go out there and scan that damn thing

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:05.520
if it was just going to eat more reaper leviathans?

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.700
I mean the enemy in my enemy might be my friend

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.860
but this guy doesn't seem to have any friends at all.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.840
And I think if I go near him he's just gonna kill me

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.420
over and over again.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.800
So anyway, he's out there, and I think my lights are off,

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.800
Uuuh, not that that's gonna help anyway.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.800
So, that's a terrifying thought.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:27.280
Also, to Noah Dawson who said something that just made me laugh,

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.820
"Don't shamwoozle the bamboozle"

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:33.320
which I think is life lessons for everybody out there.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:35.800
And then Swag Potato who said,

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.800
"Mark in a nutshell: So that was really stupid. I'm gonna go do it again,"

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:45.800
which does apply because I went back out into the cold to take pictures of myself

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:51.800
with less and less clothing progressively throughout the day, which is probably why I'm sick.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:55.800
But then again, everybody got sick from that PAX and this was a particularly bad one.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.800
So, with that being said I'm gonna let you guys know what my plan is and right now,

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:02.900
my plan is to get the hecky away from wherever the hell that dragon is.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.800
I hope he's not immediately below me, because that's where I'm gonna go.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.800
Well shit. No I'm not.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.460
It is re-god-damn dark out down here.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:17.820
Okay, yeesh. Someone's unhappy with meeee.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.400
Okay, so what I'm gonna do down here--

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.400
Oh, I might as well make it right by this skeleton.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.400
You know, I might have a nice lawn ornament--

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.400
So when I said I was gonna be moving into the neighborhood, that means exactly what

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:32.400
you think it means. I'm going to be building a base down here, and make it my new home.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.400
I'm never-ever gonna have to leave.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.120
I've got seeds with which to plant trees.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:41.360
Hopefully there's titanium down here but who knows about that.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.800
Maybe the titanium's all melted down because of the LAVA.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.680
But imma try my best and that's all I can hope to do.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.360
So I'm gonna scow--oh hey

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.320
At least I've got my friendly neighborhood Warper.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.700
You frickin' douchebag.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:57.320
So what I need to do...

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:01.860
is I need to scout an amicable location for my base--

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:02.600
(To Warper) Aw thanks!

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.820
He doesn't like this place, the heat gets to him--

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.320
And then once I do that,

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:10.880
of which it's going to be boiling hot so I gotta take my ah,

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:12.440
my Mr. Fister here

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:13.920
I'm gonna...

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.180
Start gathering materials!

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:17.200
(Computer) Welcome aboard Captain

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:23.700
Which is my favorite thing to do in the middle of a death-defying area where there's

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.540
Dragons abound...

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:26.880
..and Warpers--

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:27.620
Why?

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.300
Oh god dammit!

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.320
It's doing that thing again!

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:36.300
It's doing that thing again where it doesn't have the pressure modulator on it and I don't know why!

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:38.200
Frickin bugs.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:40.200
Alright so I gotta access the uh...

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:42.520
I gotta access the upgrade hatch somehow.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:43.560
Frick.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.060
I guess I just gotta hop in there, get out, and do it.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.880
Alright, you know what, Imma go for it.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:50.760
Here we go!

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:53.640
Hibbidy hobbidy hibbidy hobbidy HIIB (fart noise)

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.140
Okay, so we just gotta pop this b-

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.540
Ow my skin is burning.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.600
That's great, that's good for ya.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.340
So we gotta pop this back in and out here,

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.040
and I'm going to umm

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.080
Nah, that's good enough for me.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.120
Oh, I'm burning alive!

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:06.660
Get- NOO that's not what I want.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:07.940
Can you not do that?  That'd be good.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.780
Okay, thank you for that.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:14.080
Alright, so now that my pressure, for some reason, is magically now appropriate,

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.680
I'm gonna explore this hellscape and call it:

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:17.520
Home.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:18.660
Ah, yes,

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:20.220
Lovely.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.460
I'm sure he died fun.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:23.500
What is this?

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:24.800
Is that uh...

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.140
Uh, that's diamond.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:29.600
That's not what I want.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.100
Can I get some titanium out of this sunabitch?

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.200
Nope!

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.060
Okay, this might be--

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.360
This might be a--

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.620
This might be a lost cause trying to do this.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:44.500
But if there's one thing that Markiplier doesn't do, it's give up,

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.720
especially when it's a stupid idea.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:50.120
So I'm gonna keep hammering away at this stupid idea,

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.560
until I find a source of titanium,

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:53.840
with which I can...

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:55.620
build a base...

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:56.580
(Low Grunting Noise)

00:05:57.140 --> 00:06:00.520
I hate this place. I hate everything about this place.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:03.700
And supposedly I'm nearby the uh,

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:05.040
I'm nearby- oh

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:07.240
*Sea Dragon roar*

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.900
Apparently I'm nearby--oh

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.360
That guy is mad.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.140
That guy is REAL mad.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:13.560
oohh

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:14.320
Well that is--

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:15.780
Hey is that a skull?

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:16.680
Heh, that'd be a nice--

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.460
That'd be a nice thing to wake up next to every morning and look at.

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:22.700
Oh that's beautiful-- and laggy.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:24.660
Ahhh.

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:27.400
Two frames a second, my favorite.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:28.300
There we go.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.540
Ugh, that one's infected with the Carar.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:32.100
So yeah, I'm uh-

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:37.260
yeah, okay, I've uh got no hope is basically-

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:40.300
Get out of my face, you wanna get some suckage?

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:43.100
Go suck away somewhere else, ya asshole.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:45.920
Alright, I can't-- (referring to Dragon) I don't know where that guy is,

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.640
but I can't wait to try to fall asleep to those sounds.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:52.480
Just a Sea Dragon screaming in the distance as loud as it can.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:53.940
Ugh, what is this?
*Sea Dragon roars*

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:56.320
Where is this?

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:58.640
Where is this going?

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:01.020
Oh, quit moanin'!

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:04.900
I've got the FLU, you think I care about YOUR problems?

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.700
Not you guys, his problem.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:09.740
Man, you are just a whiny bitch today!

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:12.220
Can you just-

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:16.000
M-M-M-M-Man or woman up, whatever you are

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.360
and then just be brave?

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.160
Sto- wo, Hey, WOH, WOH!

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.820
What the hell was that?

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:23.560
Excuse you!

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.320
Don't make me scan you.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.000
I'll do it, I'm brave like that.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:28.120
You want me to scan you..?

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.600
HOWH-I bet u don't I bet u just shy......

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:30.360
Hurh

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:33.900
(Sarcastic Tone) Oh, no! You took a bite! Oh, it did almost something!

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:36.600
Oh ow! Ooh! Oh yeah that hurt.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.440
*Fake moans*

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:40.060
I need to repair this thing.

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:42.100
Maybe he was hurting me, I have no idea.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:44.400
OH GOD HE IS, OKAY, HE HURTS ME! OKAY!

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:46.460
YOU KNOW WHAT I'M GONNA GRIND YOU!

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:47.740
Yeesh.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.020
Okay, that guy hurt a lot...

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:53.640
Don't you even frickin dare destroy this thing, IT'S ALL I HAVE!

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:55.760
YEEEEEE IT'S ALL I HAVE, DON'T HIT ME!

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.040
Aww come on!

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.600
Why is someone such a whiny baby?!

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:04.860
Man! He's whining up a storm!

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.120
Holy shit that guy is grumpy!

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:11.240
Ohhhh, he's up there-

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.100
Are there two of them? Are they mating!?

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:17.880
Is there a mating ritual going on of Sea Dragons of epic proportions that I don't want to be around for?

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:20.780
Uhhh, Alright, pull me in.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:23.300
Come on!

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:25.900
No, that's, that's the stupid way to do it.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:30.080
Nah, that's the outside. I like how you missed the hole there, that was good!

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.900
Lag's perfect-- yeah that's it!

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:33.980
Hupp!

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:37.580
Yeah we made it, okay we'll call that one a good.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:38.440
Ooohh.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:40.160
Oh.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:41.640
Hang on, wait a second.

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:44.460
Alien thermal plant!

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.880
Oh! I am right by it!

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:50.080
Oh, you know, I might as well go over there...

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:53.880
Might as well skedaddle and see what that's all about, because that's gotta be fun!

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:56.780
A whole plant dedicated to thermal!

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:57.740
Huh!

00:08:57.880 --> 00:08:58.840
Can you umm...

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:01.820
If you're gonna be here then I might as well name you!

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.320
I'm gonna call you...

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:04.580
Little...

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.540
Li- Little Larva Larry.

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:11.500
Nah, I named a lot of things Larry, I don't wanna name you Larry too...

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:12.840
I'm gonna call you...

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:17.620
Little Lar- Little Larva Lester!

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:20.760
After my Favorite Youtuber Phil Lester.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:23.540
So far I'm just skirting around this big spiral-

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:27.780
I honestly didn't know that I was fighting over in that- the big pillars of smoke were

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:30.180
the exhaust tubes for the thermal plant.

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:33.880
So what I gotta do is I gotta find the entrance wherever the hell it is.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:34.720
*Mumbling* I don't even know-

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:38.300
I don't even know how I got these co-ordinates. They were just in my inventory.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.980
What do you think, Lester? Huh?

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:43.300
Little Larva Lester! Oh, you're gonna be a plushie soon!

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:45.920
Everyone is gonna have this horrible thing that will just suck...

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:47.360
All the power out of them.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:48.480
Nah, that's a bad idea!

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.940
Nooo, hey, okay.

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:52.860
That was a thing that happened.

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:55.380
OHH I'M IN THE MIDDLE OF A DRAGON!

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:56.940
I didn't realize that!

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.400
Ohh, okay, sorry, excuse me.

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:01.580
Please do not bat me around

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.400
you can't hurt me. I'm in my-

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:05.600
Oh hey, okay.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:06.760
Alright, that was weird.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:09.480
Okay so maybe I was on the correct side.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.940
Is there something, oooh wait I see something up there!

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:13.080
Ahhhhh!

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:14.500
HELLO, HELLO, HELLO!

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.160
My name is Markiplier!

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:17.520
... How are you doing?

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:18.900
Ahh yes!

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.680
I will enter this weird...

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:26.060
Geologically bizarre place.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:31.180
Okay, Alright then. I wish I could repair my doodydadder, that'd be awfully nice.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:32.300
But I can't.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.740
And my inventory is full, why is my inventory full?

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:37.400
I gotta drop off some shit.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.180
Argh, I keep wasting my time like this.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:41.240
Okay, so we're gonna go into this bad boy.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:45.600
and then I'm going to do what I need to do, and if I need a key I'm going to be screwed,

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.620
because I don't think I have enough diamond for that...

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:50.140
OH WHAT AM I TALKING ABOUT. There is diamond everywhere here.

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:53.120
This is literally the only place where diamond is in excess.

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:54.240
So...

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.120
I- I'm gonna make that if I need to make that-

00:10:56.120 --> 00:11:00.920
but I don't know if I need to make that yet, so I'm gonna hold off on that until I KNOW I need to make that.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:04.420
Then I'm gonna take Mr. Fister in there and hopefully repair him on the way out.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:05.580
LET'S DO THIS!!!

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:07.380
Come on!!!!

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:08.800
I'm ready for ya.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.620
WE'RE ready for it.

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:11.800
Whatever's in here--

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:12.300
Whoa 'kay.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.580
Alright, faster than I thought.

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:15.220
Okie dokie!

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:16.800
Love the decor!

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:18.160
Ahhh...

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:19.880
This looks horrifying.

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:21.680
Oh goody!

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:23.580
I hope I die here!

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:26.240
Ahhhh

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.260
*Sea Dragon roars*

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:29.960
I see it's haunted by the screams of the damned.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:31.780
Woah woah, laggy...

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:33.880
Almost sent me into the abyss!

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:35.420
Okay then...

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:38.120
Well this is promising!

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:40.220
So...

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:42.120
I'm in here-

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:44.100
but what else is in here?

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.040
Oh, it just keeps going down.

